# Logging

The general logging rules. Domain-specific namespaces extend this rather than
restate it — see [[/specs/auth/logging|the authentication variant]].

Every request carries a correlation id, propagated unchanged across service
boundaries. ^correlation-id

## Levels

| Level | Use |
| --- | --- |
| `error` | the request failed and the caller must act |
| `warn` | the request succeeded through a fallback |
| `info` | one line per completed request |

## Redaction

Structured fields are redacted by key, never by pattern-matching the rendered
line. A pattern that matches a secret today matches a different substring after
the next format change.

!!! warning "No credentials in logs"

    Bearer tokens, refresh tokens, and signing keys MUST NOT reach a log sink,
    including in error paths.
